import Mathlib

/-!
# Automorphisms of Cuntz algebra

Source: https://mathoverflow.net/questions/236762
Credit: @adammcarter

The question (MathOverflow 236762, by DLN). Let `O_∞` be the Cuntz algebra, the C*-algebra generated
by isometries `S_i` (`i ∈ ℕ`) with `S_i^* S_j = δ_ij`. The span of the products `S_i S_j` is a Hilbert
space `H` with inner product `⟨u, v⟩ 1 = v^* u`. Given a unitary `U : H → H` that commutes with the
flip `σ` (`σ (S_i S_j) = S_j S_i`), is there an automorphism `φ` of `O_∞` with `φ x = U x` for all
`x ∈ H`?

Reading choices (each one is the standard reading of the source):
* `O_∞`: we quantify over every complex C*-algebra `A` with a family `S : ℕ → A` such that
  `star (S i) * S j = if i = j then 1 else 0` and the closed *-subalgebra generated by the `S i` is
  all of `A`. By Cuntz's uniqueness theorem (Cuntz 1977, `O_∞` is simple) every nonzero such `A` is
  canonically isomorphic to `O_∞` with `S i ↦ S_i`, and the property asked about is invariant under
  such isomorphisms. (The zero algebra also satisfies the relations; there the claim holds trivially.)
* `H`: the source calls the span a Hilbert space, so `H` is the closed linear span of the `S i * S j`.
  The source's inner product gives `⟨u, u⟩ = ‖u‖^2` (C*-identity), so this closure is the right one.
* Unitary: a complex-linear bijection `U` of `H` that preserves the source's inner product,
  written exactly as in the source: `star (U v) * U u = star v * u`.
* Flip: `σ` is the unique bounded linear map of `H` with `σ (S i * S j) = S j * S i`. It exists (it is a
  unitary of `H`), so instead of constructing it we quantify over every bounded linear `σ` with this
  property; that is equivalent, as such a `σ` is unique.
* Automorphism: a *-automorphism of the C*-algebra (`A ≃⋆ₐ[ℂ] A`), the meaning in operator algebras.

The question is yes/no, so `main` states the YES answer: every flip-commuting unitary of `H`
extends to an automorphism. The poster suspects the answer is NO (no automorphism seemed to exist
for `U = σ`); that is `¬ main`. The follow-up requests in the source (a characterization of the
good unitaries, and references) are not part of this statement.
-/

namespace OMA.S_mo_236762

/-- `S` satisfies the relations of the Cuntz algebra `O_∞` and generates `A` as a C*-algebra. -/
def IsCuntzInfinityFamily {A : Type*} [CStarAlgebra A] (S : ℕ → A) : Prop :=
  (∀ i j, star (S i) * S j = if i = j then 1 else 0) ∧
    (StarAlgebra.adjoin ℂ (Set.range S)).topologicalClosure = ⊤

/-- The Hilbert space `H`: the closed linear span of the products `S i * S j`. -/
noncomputable def quadSpace {A : Type*} [CStarAlgebra A] (S : ℕ → A) : Submodule ℂ A :=
  (Submodule.span ℂ (Set.range fun p : ℕ × ℕ => S p.1 * S p.2)).topologicalClosure

theorem main :
    ∀ (A : Type) [CStarAlgebra A] (S : ℕ → A), IsCuntzInfinityFamily S →
      ∀ (U : quadSpace S ≃ₗ[ℂ] quadSpace S),
        (∀ u v : quadSpace S, star (U v : A) * (U u : A) = star (v : A) * (u : A)) →
      ∀ (σ : quadSpace S →L[ℂ] quadSpace S),
        (∀ (x : quadSpace S) (i j : ℕ), (x : A) = S i * S j → (σ x : A) = S j * S i) →
        (∀ x : quadSpace S, U (σ x) = σ (U x)) →
      ∃ φ : A ≃⋆ₐ[ℂ] A, ∀ x : quadSpace S, φ (x : A) = (U x : A) := by
  sorry

end OMA.S_mo_236762
